unset. A value other than the ones listed is treated as unset rather than
refused.

| Setting | Values | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `DECKO_SHADOW_VIEW_LANE` | `1` turns it on | Off | Node host: a page request with a `view` parameter is answered by the bare view renderer instead of the full page path, which changes the answer for a view the deck does not support (the full page path answers 422). The project's shadow comparison tool, which is not part of this package, sets it on the hosts it starts. |
| `DECKO_LEGACY_RULE_CLOSURE` | `1` turns it on | Off | The render path's rule-closure walk runs the older reference SQL statement instead of the narrower statement it normally runs, which returns the same rows. Kept for measurement. |
| `DECKO_LEGACY_RULE_UNIVERSE` | `1` turns it on | Off | Rule lookups by setting run the earlier whole-deck top-down SQL walk instead of the upward walk. Kept for measurement. |
| `DECKO_ONE_TRIP`, `DECKO_ONE_TRIP_STORE`, `DECKO_ONE_TRIP_PLANS` | `DECKO_ONE_TRIP`: `1` turns it on. `DECKO_ONE_TRIP_STORE`: the path of a side database, or `inline`. `DECKO_ONE_TRIP_PLANS`: `0` turns plans off | `DECKO_ONE_TRIP` off; no store; plans on | `DECKO_ONE_TRIP=1` makes a page render fetch a precomputed page bundle and replay stored render plans instead of discovering its reads one by one. The bundle comes from the store `DECKO_ONE_TRIP_STORE` names: a side database the engine attaches, or `inline` for `one_trip_*` tables in the serving database. The store must be built beforehand; a render never builds it. `DECKO_ONE_TRIP_PLANS=0` leaves stored render plans out of that fetch. Off by default, so a default deployment reads none of these tables. |
