| `DECKO_WARMUP_LINKS_SPINE` | `1` turns it on | Off | During render warm-up, the target of a `[[link]]` is prepared without its own references being scanned, unless a nest, list item or navigation bar reaches it. `1` restores the older scan through link targets. Read once when the module loads. |
| `DECKO_ENGINE_NEST_TRACE` | `1` turns it on | Off | Writes one trace line per nest render to standard output. Read once when the module loads. |
| `DECKO_LIVE_*` (26 names: `DECKO_LIVE_ALL_RULES`, `_ANCHOR_LEFTS`, `_ASKED_LEFTS`, `_AUTO_TAIL`, `_AUTO_THRESHOLD`, `_COMPACT`, `_DEBUG`, `_DENIED_CLOSURE`, `_FIRST_GLOBALS`, `_IDENTITY_RING`, `_INCREMENTAL`, `_INCREMENTAL_LEVEL`, `_INCREMENTAL_SWEEP`, `_KEEP`, `_PARTIAL`, `_RING_ALL`, `_RULE_SETS`, `_RULE_SETS_SELF`, `_SET_HINTS`, `_SIDES_SCAN`, `_STAR_FULL`, `_STRUCTURE_WALKS`, `_TRACE`, `_TRACE_ROWS`, `_TRACE_RULESETS`, `_TRACE_STACK`) | Mostly `1` to turn a behaviour on or `0` to turn a default behaviour off; `_AUTO_TAIL`, `_AUTO_THRESHOLD`, `_INCREMENTAL_LEVEL` and `_TRACE_STACK` take numbers | Each switch's own default | Read by the engine's live render path (src/card/live/), which selects how a page's database reads are batched, encoded, kept between requests and traced. The project's hosted edge entry, which is not part of this package, uses that path; no host in this package calls it, so these settings have no effect on the Node host. |
